### Closira API — HTTP Test File
### Compatible with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### Install: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 1 — Submit a new inbound WhatsApp enquiry about pricing
# Expected: 202 Accepted | { enquiry_id, status: "open", message }
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# @name submitEnquiry
POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_name": "Sarah Mitchell",
  "channel": "whatsapp",
  "message": "Hi, I wanted to know about your pricing plans for small businesses"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 2 — Submit a complaint via email (will trigger auto-escalation if
#           background task runs before this comment is reached)
# Expected: 202 Accepted
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_name": "James O'Brien",
  "channel": "email",
  "message": "I am really disappointed with the service. I want a refund immediately."
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 3 — Submit a booking enquiry via phone
# Expected: 202 Accepted | background task should match "Booking Enquiry" SOP
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_name": "Priya Sharma",
  "channel": "call",
  "message": "Hi, I'd like to book an appointment for next Tuesday morning if possible"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 4 — Schedule a follow-up on Sarah's enquiry
# Replace <enquiry_id> with the enquiry_id from STEP 1's response
# Expected: 201 Created | followup record with scheduled_at
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@sarahEnquiryId = <enquiry_id>

POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/{{sarahEnquiryId}}/followup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delay_minutes": 30,
  "message_template": "Hi {customer_name}, just following up on your pricing enquiry. Let us know if you have any questions!"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 5 — Schedule a follow-up using the default template (no message_template)
# Expected: 201 Created | message_template populated with system default
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/{{sarahEnquiryId}}/followup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delay_minutes": 60
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 6 — Manually escalate Sarah's enquiry
# Expected: 200 OK | status: "escalated", escalation_reason populated
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/{{sarahEnquiryId}}/escalate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Customer called back frustrated — escalating to senior support for immediate callback"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 7 — Attempt to escalate again (should fail with 409 Conflict)
# Expected: 409 Conflict | error: "enquiry_already_escalated"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/{{sarahEnquiryId}}/escalate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Trying to escalate again"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 8 — Retrieve full history for Sarah's enquiry
# Expected: 200 OK | enquiry + timeline (enquiry_created, followup_scheduled x2,
#           escalated) + followups list
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GET {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/{{sarahEnquiryId}}/history

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 9 — History for a non-existent enquiry
# Expected: 404 Not Found | error: "enquiry_not_found"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GET {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/history

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 10 — Health check
# Expected: 200 OK | { status: "ok", database: "connected", timestamp }
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EDGE CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Invalid channel — should return 422 with validation_error
POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_name": "Test User",
  "channel": "telegram",
  "message": "Hello from Telegram"
}

###

# Followup on non-existent enquiry — should return 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/enquiry/not-a-real-id/followup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delay_minutes": 30
}
